      "title": "공식 카탈로그 · 3쪽",
      "text": "Low Vision\nLow vision is caused by diseases such as cataracts, \nwhich cloud the lens, macular degeneration, which \ndamages central vision, and glaucoma, which affects \nthe optic nerve. Retinal diseases like diabetic \nretinopathy, along with congenital abnormalities, \ngenetic factors, and trauma, also contribute.  \nKey symptoms include tunnel vision, blurry or \ndistorted vision, light sensitivity, night blindness, and \ndifficulty distinguishing objects or letters. Reduced \ncolor discrimination and double vision may also occur.\nWHO reports that around ��� million people globally \nhave low vision, with aging increasing the prevalence \nof conditions like macular degeneration and glaucoma.\nCauses & Symptoms\n"
